Subject: [PATCH 02045/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A4
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; gated_on
 A1 family_split_feasible==true) -- Tier-1 ONLINE verifier-weight adaptation
 across the family folds. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning
 experiment per milestone; Tier 1 (online weight/counter updates, CPU,
 <1us/update, NOT the retired live-LoRA fine-tuning) is the practical tier.
 QUESTION: does cheap online adaptation recover cross-family headroom the
 STATIC selector loses? On each held-out family, compare the STATIC
 set-encoder selector vs an ONLINE-reweighted selector that upweights
 features/sub-verifiers which selected correctly on the nearest SEEN family
 (running per-feature precision, updated as families stream in). Report
 static_cross_family_delta vs online_cross_family_delta + the per-family
 adaptation curve + CI95 on the (online - static) gain. A positive gain = the
 verifier self-improves toward generalization (north-star-grade self-learning
 evidence). A null = static is the ceiling (honest, decision-grade).
 verifier_is_oracle=false. NO fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA.

